---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Ten minutes of attack on a login service" hint="20,000 accounts, 1,500 real users logging in, and one attacker. Pick the attack, pick the defence and the hashing cost, and watch who gets in, who gets locked out and how hot the login servers run.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>The default is <b>credential stuffing</b> against a <b>per-IP rate limit</b>: <b>1,949 accounts</b> are still taken, because 10,000 bot addresses send only two or three tries each. The limit only hurts real users: <b>18</b> were refused, mostly people behind shared office or mobile addresses.</li>
    <li>Switch the attacker to <b>one IP brute force</b>. A per-IP limit or a <b>per-account lockout</b> stops it, but lockout also <b>locks 99 real accounts</b> that the attacker chose as targets. The defence became the attack.</li>
    <li>Choose <b>password spraying</b> with <b>lockout</b>. After 5 failures it does nothing (3 passwords per account never reach 5). Lower the threshold to <b>3</b> and the attacker locks <b>19,861</b> accounts, about the whole user base.</li>
    <li>Go back to stuffing and pick <b>MFA</b>: <b>1,140</b> accounts are saved because the password alone is not enough. <b>Layered</b> defences cut the 1,949 to <b>96</b>. Then go back to the per-IP limit and set the hash cost to <b>very heavy</b>: the login servers run at 144% of their CPU and refuse 464 real users.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg abb" data-abb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Attacker <select class="pg-in" data-atk>
        <option value="brute">One IP brute force (100 accounts, 300 guesses each)</option>
        <option value="stuff" selected>Botnet credential stuffing (leaked pairs)</option>
        <option value="spray">Password spraying (top 3 passwords, all accounts)</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Defence <select class="pg-in" data-def>
        <option value="none">None</option>
        <option value="ip" selected>Per-IP rate limit (10 tries per 10 min)</option>
        <option value="lock">Per-account lockout</option>
        <option value="risk">Risk-based challenge (CAPTCHA)</option>
        <option value="mfa">MFA (60% of accounts enrolled)</option>
        <option value="breached">Breached-password screening</option>
        <option value="layered">Layered: IP limit, risk, MFA, screening, no hard lockout</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Password hash cost <select class="pg-in" data-cost>
        <option value="40">Light, 40 ms per check</option>
        <option value="100" selected>Standard, 100 ms per check</option>
        <option value="400">Very heavy, 400 ms per check</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Lock after N failures <input type="range" min="3" max="10" value="5" data-thr /> <b data-thrval></b></label>
      <label>Risk sensitivity <select class="pg-in" data-sens>
        <option value="low">Low</option>
        <option value="med" selected>Medium</option>
        <option value="high">High</option>
      </select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Accounts compromised</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Real users locked out or refused</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Login CPU at the busiest minute</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Real logins challenged</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: 10 minutes, 20,000 accounts, 1,500 real users who each log in once (8% mistype and retry up to twice), 12 CPU cores, and 20% of users behind 40 shared addresses. 10% of accounts use a very common password and 12% reuse a leaked one. The brute-force guesses go down a ranked list of 10,000 passwords, spraying tries the top 3, and stuffing tries 1 or 2 leaked pairs for 80% of accounts. Bots send 50 (brute force), 40 (stuffing) and 100 (spraying) requests per second. Lockout lasts the whole window, and a locked account is refused before any hashing. Risk scoring flags 95% (brute force), 65% (stuffing) and 55% (spraying) of bot requests at medium sensitivity (low and high scale that by 0.6 and 1.3) and 1.5%, 4% or 12% of real logins. Bots pass a challenge 10% of the time, people 92%. MFA protects the 60% of accounts that enrolled, and screening turns 70% of weak or reused passwords into unique ones. Above 100% CPU, a share of real logins time out. A stolen hash table is cost ÷ 40 ms times slower to crack offline.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-abb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    // MODEL START
    const USERS = 20000; const WINDOW = 600; const CORES = 12; const LEGIT = 1500; const IPLIM = 10;
    const SEED = 7; const RANK_SPAN = 10000; // a weak password's rank in the attacker's guess list, skewed to the top
    const MAX_TRIES = 3; const TYPO_RATE = 0.08; const RETRY_S = 15; // a real user mistypes, then retries 15 s later
    const BF_TARGETS = 100; const TARGET_STRIDE = 197; const BF_TRIES = 30000; // one-IP brute force: accounts hit, spacing of their ids, guesses
    const SPRAY_TRIES = 60000; const BOT_IPS = 10000; // spraying guesses; botnet address pool
    const BREACH_COVER = 0.8; // share of accounts whose credentials appear in the stuffing list
    const COMMON_SHARE = 0.1; const REUSED_UPTO = 0.22; // 10% common passwords, the next 12% reused from a breach
    const SCREEN_CATCH = 0.7; const MFA_SHARE = 0.6; // breached-password screening catches 70%; 60% enrol in MFA
    const NAT_SHARE = 0.2; const NAT_IP_BASE = 100000; const NAT_POOLS = 40; const HOME_IP_BASE = 200000; // users behind shared addresses; fake IP numbering
    const MAX_DET = 0.99; const LEGIT_PASS = 0.92; const BOT_PASS = 0.1; // risk scoring: detection cap; challenge pass rates
    const BUCKET_S = 60; const BUCKETS = WINDOW / BUCKET_S; const CORE_MS_PER_BUCKET = BUCKET_S * 1000; // CPU load per minute
    let seed = SEED; const rnd = (): number => ((seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296) / 4294967296);
    const acc = Array.from({ length: USERS }, () => ({ u: rnd(), rank: 1 + Math.floor(RANK_SPAN * Math.pow(rnd(), 3)), screen: rnd(), mfa: rnd(), nat: rnd(), cov: rnd(), two: rnd() }));
    const order = Array.from({ length: USERS }, (_, i) => i);
    for (let i = 0; i < LEGIT; i++) { const j = i + Math.floor(rnd() * (USERS - i)); const t = order[i]; order[i] = order[j]; order[j] = t; }
    const legit: any[] = [];
    for (let k = 0; k < LEGIT; k++) {
      const a = order[k]; let t = rnd() * WINDOW;
      for (let tr = 0; tr < MAX_TRIES; tr++) { const typo = rnd() < TYPO_RATE; legit.push({ t, acct: a, legit: true, correct: !typo, draw: rnd(), flag: rnd(), pass: rnd() }); if (!typo) break; t += RETRY_S; }
    }
    const bf: any[] = []; const sp: any[] = []; const st: any[] = [];
    const targets = Array.from({ length: BF_TARGETS }, (_, i) => (i * TARGET_STRIDE) % USERS);
    for (let i = 0; i < BF_TRIES; i++) bf.push({ t: (i / BF_TRIES) * WINDOW, acct: targets[i % BF_TARGETS], guess: Math.floor(i / BF_TARGETS) + 1, ip: 0, flag: rnd(), pass: rnd() });
    for (let i = 0; i < SPRAY_TRIES; i++) sp.push({ t: (i / SPRAY_TRIES) * WINDOW, acct: i % USERS, guess: Math.floor(i / USERS) + 1, ip: 1 + Math.floor(rnd() * BOT_IPS), flag: rnd(), pass: rnd() });
    for (let a = 0; a < USERS; a++) {
      if (acc[a].cov < BREACH_COVER) { const n = acc[a].two < 0.5 ? 2 : 1; for (let k = 1; k <= n; k++) st.push({ t: rnd() * WINDOW, acct: a, guess: k, last: k === n, ip: 1 + Math.floor(rnd() * BOT_IPS), flag: rnd(), pass: rnd() }); }
    }
    const DET: Record<string, number> = { brute: 0.95, stuff: 0.65, spray: 0.55 };
    const SENS: Record<string, number[]> = { low: [0.6, 0.015], med: [1, 0.04], high: [1.3, 0.12] };
    const run = (attacker: string, defence: string, cost: number, thr: number, sens: string) => {
      const on = { ip: defence === 'ip' || defence === 'layered', lock: defence === 'lock', risk: defence === 'risk' || defence === 'layered', mfa: defence === 'mfa' || defence === 'layered', screen: defence === 'breached' || defence === 'layered' };
      const type = (a: number) => { const A = acc[a]; let t = A.u < COMMON_SHARE ? 'common' : A.u < REUSED_UPTO ? 'reused' : 'strong'; if (on.screen && t !== 'strong' && A.screen < SCREEN_CATCH) t = 'strong'; return t; };
      const hasMfa = (a: number) => on.mfa && acc[a].mfa < MFA_SHARE;
      const atk = (attacker === 'brute' ? bf : attacker === 'spray' ? sp : st).map((e) => ({ ...e, legit: false }));
      const ev = [...legit.map((e) => ({ ...e, ip: acc[e.acct].nat < NAT_SHARE ? NAT_IP_BASE + (e.acct % NAT_POOLS) : HOME_IP_BASE + e.acct })), ...atk].sort((a, b) => a.t - b.t);
      const dm = SENS[sens][0]; const fp = SENS[sens][1]; const det = Math.min(MAX_DET, DET[attacker] * dm);
      const ipc = new Map<number, number>(); const fails = new Map<number, number>(); const locked = new Set<number>(); const cracked = new Set<number>(); const comp = new Set<number>(); const mfaStop = new Set<number>();
      const hashed = new Array(BUCKETS).fill(0); const denied = new Set<number>(); let legitAtt = 0; let flagged = 0; const okLegit: any[] = [];
      for (const e of ev) {
        if (!e.legit && cracked.has(e.acct)) continue;
        let ok = true;
        if (on.ip) { const c = (ipc.get(e.ip) || 0) + 1; ipc.set(e.ip, c); if (c > IPLIM) ok = false; }
        if (ok && on.lock && locked.has(e.acct)) ok = false;
        if (ok && on.risk) { const f = e.legit ? e.flag < fp : e.flag < det; if (f) { if (e.legit) flagged++; const p = e.legit ? e.pass < LEGIT_PASS : e.pass < BOT_PASS; if (!p) ok = false; } }
        if (e.legit) legitAtt++;
        if (!ok) { if (e.legit) denied.add(e.acct); continue; }
        hashed[Math.min(BUCKETS - 1, Math.floor(e.t / BUCKET_S))] += cost;
        let correct: boolean;
        if (e.legit) correct = e.correct; else { const t = type(e.acct); correct = attacker === 'stuff' ? t === 'reused' && e.last : t === 'common' && acc[e.acct].rank === e.guess; }
        if (!correct) { const f = (fails.get(e.acct) || 0) + 1; fails.set(e.acct, f); if (on.lock && f >= thr) locked.add(e.acct); }
        else if (!e.legit) { cracked.add(e.acct); if (hasMfa(e.acct)) mfaStop.add(e.acct); else comp.add(e.acct); }
        else okLegit.push(e);
      }
      const loads = hashed.map((h) => h / (CORE_MS_PER_BUCKET * CORES)); const peak = Math.max(...loads);
      let overDen = 0;
      for (const e of okLegit) { const l = loads[Math.min(BUCKETS - 1, Math.floor(e.t / BUCKET_S))]; if (l > 1 && e.draw > 1 / l) { denied.add(e.acct); overDen++; } }
      const lockedLegit = [...locked].filter((a) => !comp.has(a));
      const refused = new Set<number>([...lockedLegit, ...denied]).size;
      return { comp: comp.size, mfaStop: mfaStop.size, locked: lockedLegit.length, denied: denied.size, refused, peak, flagRate: flagged / legitAtt, overDen, legitAtt };
    };
    // MODEL END
    const fmt = (n: number) => Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-US');
    const MANY_TAKEN = 50; const FEW_REFUSED = 25; const MANY_REFUSED = 500; // verdict thresholds, accounts
    const CPU_WARN = 0.7; const FLAG_BAD = 0.08; // CPU share that warns; share of real logins challenged that is too much friction
    const BASE_COST_MS = 40; // reference hashing cost
    const ATK: Record<string, string> = { brute: 'one IP brute force', stuff: 'botnet credential stuffing', spray: 'password spraying' };
    function draw() {
      const atk = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-atk]').value; const def = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-def]').value; const cost = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-cost]').value);
      const thr = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-thr]').value); const sens = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-sens]').value;
      q('[data-thrval]').textContent = String(thr);
      q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-thr]').disabled = def !== 'lock';
      q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-sens]').disabled = !(def === 'risk' || def === 'layered');
      const r = run(atk, def, cost, thr, sens);
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = `${fmt(r.comp)} of ${fmt(USERS)}`;
      q('[data-n1]').textContent = r.mfaStop > 0 ? `${fmt(r.mfaStop)} more had their password guessed but MFA stopped the login` : 'accounts where the attacker got a session';
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = fmt(r.refused);
      q('[data-n2]').textContent = `${fmt(r.locked)} accounts locked by failures; ${fmt(r.denied)} of the ${fmt(LEGIT)} people who tried to log in were refused`;
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = `${Math.round(r.peak * 100)}%`;
      q('[data-n3]').textContent = `${CORES} cores at ${cost} ms per password check${r.peak > 1 ? `, so ${fmt(r.overDen)} real logins timed out` : ''}`;
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = `${(r.flagRate * 100).toFixed(1)}%`;
      q('[data-n4]').textContent = def === 'risk' || def === 'layered' ? 'of real login attempts were sent to a CAPTCHA or step-up' : 'no risk scoring, so nobody is challenged';
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b1]').style.setProperty('--c', r.comp === 0 ? 'var(--good)' : r.comp < MANY_TAKEN ? 'var(--accent)' : 'var(--bad)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b2]').style.setProperty('--c', r.refused < FEW_REFUSED ? 'var(--good)' : r.refused < MANY_REFUSED ? 'var(--accent)' : 'var(--bad)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b3]').style.setProperty('--c', r.peak > 1 ? 'var(--bad)' : r.peak > CPU_WARN ? 'var(--accent)' : 'var(--good)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b4]').style.setProperty('--c', r.flagRate > FLAG_BAD ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--accent)');
      const bad = r.comp >= MANY_TAKEN || r.refused >= MANY_REFUSED || r.peak > 1;
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); out.classList.toggle('bad', bad);
      const parts: string[] = [];
      if (r.comp >= MANY_TAKEN) parts.push(`${fmt(r.comp)} accounts were taken by ${ATK[atk]}, and this defence does not match how that attack works.`);
      else if (r.comp > 0) parts.push(`Only ${fmt(r.comp)} account${r.comp === 1 ? ' was' : 's were'} taken.`);
      else parts.push(`No account was taken by ${ATK[atk]}.`);
      if (r.locked >= MANY_REFUSED) parts.push(`But the lockout rule locked ${fmt(r.locked)} real accounts: the attacker used your defence as a denial of service.`);
      else if (r.locked > 0) parts.push(`The lockout rule locked ${fmt(r.locked)} real accounts that the attacker targeted.`);
      if (r.peak > 1) parts.push(`The login servers were at ${Math.round(r.peak * 100)}% of their CPU, so ${fmt(r.overDen)} real logins timed out: hashing cost is also a cost to you.`);
      if (r.flagRate > FLAG_BAD) parts.push(`${(r.flagRate * 100).toFixed(0)}% of real logins were challenged, which is a lot of friction.`);
      if (def === 'ip' && r.denied > 0 && atk !== 'brute') parts.push(`The IP limit refused real users behind shared addresses and did not slow a botnet that uses a fresh address for each try.`);
      if (cost > BASE_COST_MS) parts.push(`A stolen hash table is ${cost / BASE_COST_MS} times slower to crack offline than at ${BASE_COST_MS} ms.`);
      out.textContent = parts.join(' ');
    }
    let queued = false;
    const schedule = () => { if (queued) return; queued = true; requestAnimationFrame(() => { queued = false; draw(); }); };
    root.addEventListener('input', schedule); root.addEventListener('change', schedule);
    draw();
  });
</script>
